<article class="env-corollary" id="0065">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0065">Corollary <span data-tag="0065">1.5.3.6</span>.</a> The formation of homotopy categories determines a functor $\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}\rightarrow \operatorname{Cat}$ which commutes with finite products. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since the construction $S \mapsto \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{S}$ preserves final objects, it will suffice to show that for any pair of simplicial sets $S$ and $T$, the canonical map $u: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{( S \times T)} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{S} \times \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{T}$ is an isomorphism of categories. In other words, we wish to show that for any category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, composition with $u$ induces a bijection 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Cat}}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{S} \times \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{T}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Cat}}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{(S \times T)}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}). \]
</div>
<p>
       Unwinding the definitions, we see that this map is given by the composition 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \begin{eqnarray*}  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Cat}}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{S} \times \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{T}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Cat}}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{S}, \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{T}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ) \\ &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}}( S, \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{T}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ) ) \\ &amp;  \xrightarrow {\rho _{T} \circ } &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}}( S, \operatorname{Fun}( T, \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) )) \\ &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}}( S \times T, \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) ) \\ &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Cat}}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{ (S \times T )}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}), \end{eqnarray*}
</div>
<p>
       where $\rho _{T}$ is the isomorphism appearing in the statement of Corollary <a data-tag="0064" href="/tag/0064">1.5.3.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
